script WaddleDeeTown_Lab_EventScript_Book12
{
    lockall
    msgbox("DREAM LAND: ULTIMATE JOKE BOOK!
    
            \qoQ: What do Waddle Dees carry their
            drinks in?
            
            A: Waddle bottles!
            
            Q: When the Great King was in school,
            what did his report card look like?
            
            A: D, D, D!
            
            Q: What did the grumpy tourist say
            after visiting Popstar?
            
            A: I rate this planet one star!\qc
            
            \.
            
            You'd probably be laughing if you could
            read.")
    release
}

script WaddleDeeTown_Lab_EventScript_Book13
{
    lockall
    msgbox("Artifactual: Volume 2
    
            \qoThe Fountain of Dreams is powered by
            the Star Rod (see volume 1), which some
            say also created the fountain itself.
            
            Hopes and dreams gather to and flow
            from the fountain's waters.
            
            Dreams that flow from the fountain can
            enter the minds of the slumbering.
            
            These dreams are normally pleasant,
            but can be corrupted when sinister
            intentions soak in the springs.
            
            Fountains of Dreams can be found
            on several different planets.\qc")
    release
}

script WaddleDeeTown_Lab_EventScript_Book14
{
    lockall
    msgbox("Popstar Chronicle: Volume X4
    
            \qoA dark cloud has covered the planet,
            possessing all who encounter it.
            
            Its appearance and behavior calls to
            mind the Dark Matter that appeared
            at the Rainbow Islands not long ago.
            
            Dark Matter attacked Dream Land out
            of loneliness-induced frustration\.
            
            So why does this cloud, which hosts 
            all kind of Dark Matter in it, fight?
            
            Is surrounding oneself with others not
            enough to dispel loneliness? What is?\qc")
    release
}

script WaddleDeeTown_Lab_EventScript_Book15
{
    lockall
    msgbox("Waddle Dee Fairy Tale
    
            \qo???\qc")
    release
}

script WaddleDeeTown_Lab_EventScript_Book16
{
    lockall
    msgbox("Artifactual: Volume 25
    
            \qoDream Rods can be found in palaces
            across several different planets.
            
            They bring dreams to life, which make
            them similar to wish-granting items.
            
            However, their creations are merely
            visualizations made of dream energy,
            rather than original items.
            
            As such, the Dream Rod struggles to
            conceptualize abstract dreams.\qc")
    release
}

script WaddleDeeTown_Lab_EventScript_Book18
{
    lockall
    msgbox("Popstar Chronicle: Volume XA
    
            \qoIt was all too brief, but for a moment,
            Popstar was in grave danger once more.
            
            This time, a shroud of tangled vines
            ensnared the planet, trapping its
            residents in an inescapable bind.
            
            Victims of the incident noted they felt
            their vitality being drained.
            
            The source of these vines is as of yet
            unidentified, but seemed to be high
            above the clouds\.
            
            What sort of dangerous threats could
            lurk just outside our sights?\qc")
    release
}

script WaddleDeeTown_Lab_EventScript_Book19
{
    lockall
    msgbox("Popstar Chronicle: Volume XB
    
            \qoA mysterious spaceship docked on our
            planet. Unlike last time, this one was
            large enough to overshadow the planet.
            
            From this vessel, a large workforce
            emerged and immediately took over.
            
            Large-scale mechanical terraforming
            urbanized the natural surroundings.
            
            With the vessel's explosion, the damage
            has mostly been done, but one wonders\.
            
            For all the chaos and disruption, it also
            introduced new modernizations and
            technologies to the planet.
            
            Will they ever see the light of day in
            a form that can coexist with nature?\qc")
    release
}

script WaddleDeeTown_Lab_EventScript_Book20
{
    lockall
    msgbox("Artifactual: Volume 67
    
            \qoThe Master Crown was a device said to
            grant limitless power to its wearer.

            It was known as the legendary treasure
            of Planet Halcandra, which fell into
            ruin long ago.

            How such a powerful item was unable to
            prevent the grim fate of Halcandra is
            a mystery to scholars\.\qc")
    release
}

script WaddleDeeTown_Lab_EventScript_Book21
{
    lockall
    msgbox("Helper Handbook: Stats
    
            \qoHelpers have six unique stats that
            define their abilities in combat.
            
            Their HP is the amount of damage they
            can take before being defeated.
            
            Attack and Special Attack marks the
            power of physical and special moves\.
            
            \.and Defense and Special Defense is
            their resistance to those moves.

            Incidentally, moves are classified as
            physical or special individually, rather
            than by other metrics such as type.
            
            Lastly, Helpers with higher Speed
            move before those with lower Speed.\qc")
    release
}

script WaddleDeeTown_Lab_EventScript_Book22
{
    lockall
    msgbox("Helper Handbook: Status Conditions
    
            \qoHelpers can be afflicted by several
            malignant statuses.
            
            Poison whittles a Helper's HP away
            after each turn in battle.
            
            Burns deal less damage than poison, but
            they also weaken physical blows.
            
            Paralysis slows Helper movement and
            renders them immobile occasionally.
            
            Sleep and freezing also incapacitate
            Helpers temporarily, but certain moves
            can cure the afflicted specimens.")
    release
}

script WaddleDeeTown_Lab_EventScript_Book23
{
    lockall
    msgbox("Helper Handbook: Types
    
            \qoPlease consult the following graph on
            the intricacies of the type chart.\qc
            
            \. \. \.
            
            It's too complicated to describe in
            text boxes this small\.
            
            Thankfully, battles will tell you how
            effective moves are on an enemy.
            Just rely on that instead, okay?")
    release
}

